IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 12, Division 3 (insider trading), first part: ss 213 to 217 (application, interpretation, information generally available,
-- material effect on price or value, trading and procuring). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Reading an answer and the markers are explained at the head of sfab-division-1.l4 and in NOTES.md.
-- s 214(1) "information" paragraph (c)(iii) is shown "[Deleted by Act 4 of 2017]" and is a row of the coverage table, not a rule.

§ `s 213: application of Division 3`

-- src:34896 | 213. This Division applies to —
@ref s 213 (src:34896-34896)
GIVEN
    `this Division applies to the act occurring within Singapore (the answer under section 213(a))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 213(a) answer for this act? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `this Division applies to the act occurring outside Singapore (the answer under section 213(b))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 213(b) answer for this act? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213 this Division applies to the act` MEANS
    IF (`this Division applies to the act occurring within Singapore (the answer under section 213(a))` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`this Division applies to the act occurring outside Singapore (the answer under section 213(b))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Division applies to"

-- src:34898 | (a) acts occurring within Singapore in relation to —
-- src:34900 | (i) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of
-- src:34901 | any corporation, whether formed or carrying on
-- src:34902 | business in Singapore or elsewhere;
-- src:34904 | (ii) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of
-- src:34905 | any business trust;
-- src:34910 | (iii) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:34911 | listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market
-- src:34912 | in Singapore or elsewhere;
-- src:34914 | (iv) securities‑based derivatives contracts, whether
-- src:34915 | traded in Singapore or elsewhere; or
-- src:34917 | (v) CIS units —
-- src:34919 | (A) listed for quotation or quoted on an organised
-- src:34920 | market in Singapore or elsewhere; or
-- src:34922 | (B) traded in Singapore or elsewhere; and
@ref s 213(a) (src:34898-34922)
GIVEN
    `the act occurs within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act occur within Singapore?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation, whether formed or carrying on business in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation, whether formed or carrying on business in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the act relates to securities-based derivatives contracts, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities-based derivatives contracts, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the act relates to CIS units listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to CIS units listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere?
    `the act relates to CIS units traded in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to CIS units traded in Singapore or elsewhere?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(a) this Division applies to the act occurring within Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the act occurs within Singapore` AND (`the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation, whether formed or carrying on business in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust` OR `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the act relates to securities-based derivatives contracts, whether traded in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the act relates to CIS units listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore or elsewhere` OR `the act relates to CIS units traded in Singapore or elsewhere`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "acts occurring within Singapore in relation to" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [SCOPE]

-- src:34924 | (b) acts occurring outside Singapore in relation to —
-- src:34926 | (i) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of
-- src:34927 | a corporation that is formed or carries on business in
-- src:34928 | Singapore;
-- src:34930 | (ii) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts of
-- src:34931 | a business trust, the trustee of which is formed in
-- src:34932 | Singapore or carries on business on behalf of the
-- src:34933 | business trust in Singapore;
-- src:34935 | (iii) securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:34936 | listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market
-- src:34937 | in Singapore;
-- src:34939 | (iv) securities‑based derivatives contracts traded in
-- src:34940 | Singapore; or
-- src:34942 | (v) CIS units —
-- src:34944 | (A) listed for quotation or quoted on an organised
-- src:34945 | market in Singapore; or
-- src:34947 | (B) traded in Singapore.
@ref s 213(b) (src:34924-34947)
GIVEN
    `the act occurs outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act occur outside Singapore?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation that is formed or carries on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation that is formed or carries on business in Singapore?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust, the trustee of which is formed in Singapore or carries on business on behalf of the business trust in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust, the trustee of which is formed in Singapore or carries on business on behalf of the business trust in Singapore?
    `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore?
    `the act relates to securities-based derivatives contracts traded in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to securities-based derivatives contracts traded in Singapore?
    `the act relates to CIS units listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to CIS units listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore?
    `the act relates to CIS units traded in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act relate to CIS units traded in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 213(b) this Division applies to the act occurring outside Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the act occurs outside Singapore` AND (`the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a corporation that is formed or carries on business in Singapore` OR `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts of a business trust, the trustee of which is formed in Singapore or carries on business on behalf of the business trust in Singapore` OR `the act relates to securities or securities-based derivatives contracts listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore` OR `the act relates to securities-based derivatives contracts traded in Singapore` OR `the act relates to CIS units listed for quotation or quoted on an organised market in Singapore` OR `the act relates to CIS units traded in Singapore`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "acts occurring outside Singapore in relation to" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [SCOPE]

§ `s 214: interpretation of Division 3`

-- src:34952 | 214.—(1) In this Division —
-- src:34953 | “Collective Investment Scheme unit” or “CIS unit” means —
-- src:34954 | (a) a right or interest (however described) in a collective
-- src:34955 | investment scheme (whether or not constituted as an
-- src:34960 | entity), and includes an option to acquire any such
-- src:34961 | right or interest in the collective investment scheme;
-- src:34962 | or
-- src:34964 | (b) a contract or arrangement under which —
-- src:34966 | (i) a party to the contract or arrangement is
-- src:34967 | required to, or may be required to, discharge
-- src:34968 | its obligations under the contract or
-- src:34969 | arrangement at some future time; and
-- src:34971 | (ii) the value of the contract or arrangement, is
-- src:34972 | determined (whether directly or indirectly, or
-- src:34973 | whether wholly or in part) by reference to,
-- src:34974 | derived from, or varies by reference to any of
-- src:34975 | the following:
-- src:34977 | (A) the value or amount of units of a
-- src:34978 | collective investment scheme;
-- src:34980 | (B) fluctuations in the values or amount of
-- src:34981 | units of a collective investment scheme;
@ref s 214(1) "CIS unit" (src:34952-34981)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a right or interest, however described, in a collective investment scheme, whether or not constituted as an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a right or interest (however described) in a collective investment scheme (whether or not constituted as an entity)?
    `the thing is an option to acquire such a right or interest in the collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an option to acquire such a right or interest in the collective investment scheme?
    `a party to the contract or arrangement is required to, or may be required to, discharge its obligations at some future time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a party to the contract or arrangement required to, or may it be required to, discharge its obligations under the contract or arrangement at some future time?
    `the value of the contract or arrangement is determined by reference to, derived from, or varies by reference to the value or amount of units of a collective investment scheme or fluctuations in them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the value of the contract or arrangement determined (directly or indirectly, wholly or in part) by reference to, derived from, or does it vary by reference to the value or amount of units of a collective investment scheme, or fluctuations in the values or amount of units of a collective investment scheme?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214(1) "CIS unit" the thing is a CIS unit` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a right or interest, however described, in a collective investment scheme, whether or not constituted as an entity` OR `the thing is an option to acquire such a right or interest in the collective investment scheme` OR (`a party to the contract or arrangement is required to, or may be required to, discharge its obligations at some future time` AND `the value of the contract or arrangement is determined by reference to, derived from, or varies by reference to the value or amount of units of a collective investment scheme or fluctuations in them`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Collective Investment Scheme unit” or “CIS unit” means"

-- src:34983 | “debenture” has the meaning given by section 2 and, in relation
-- src:34984 | to a business trust, means a debenture issued by the trustee of
-- src:34985 | the business trust in its capacity as trustee of the business
-- src:34986 | trust;
@ref s 214(1) "debenture" (src:34983-34986)
GIVEN
    `the instrument is a debenture as section 2 defines it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 2(1) "debenture" answer for this instrument? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the debenture is in relation to a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the debenture one in relation to a business trust?
    `the debenture was issued by the trustee of the business trust in its capacity as trustee of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the debenture issued by the trustee of the business trust in its capacity as trustee of the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214(1) "debenture" the instrument is a debenture for the purposes of this Division` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the debenture is in relation to a business trust`
        THEN `the instrument is a debenture as section 2 defines it`
        IF `the instrument is a debenture as section 2 defines it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the meaning given by section 2"
        IF NOT `the debenture was issued by the trustee of the business trust in its capacity as trustee of the business trust`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a business trust, means a debenture issued by the trustee of the business trust in its capacity as trustee of the business trust"
        IF `the instrument is a debenture as section 2 defines it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer under section 2(1) "debenture" was not given

-- src:34988 | “financial performance”, in relation to a business trust, means
-- src:34989 | the performance of the business relating to the trust property
-- src:34990 | of the business trust which is managed and operated by the
-- src:34991 | trustee of the business trust;
@ref s 214(1) "financial performance" (src:34988-34991)
GIVEN
    `the matter is the performance of the business relating to the trust property of the business trust which is managed and operated by the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the performance of the business relating to the trust property of the business trust which is managed and operated by the trustee of the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214(1) "financial performance" the matter is the financial performance of a business trust` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the performance of the business relating to the trust property of the business trust which is managed and operated by the trustee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“financial performance”, in relation to a business trust, means"

-- src:34993 | “information” includes —
-- src:34995 | (a) matters of supposition and other matters that are
-- src:34996 | insufficiently definite to warrant being made known
-- src:34997 | to the public;
-- src:34999 | (b) matters relating to the intentions, or the likely
-- src:35000 | intentions, of a person;
-- src:35002 | (c) matters relating to negotiations or proposals with
-- src:35003 | respect to —
-- src:35008 | (i) commercial dealings; or
-- src:35010 | (ii) dealing in capital markets products that are
-- src:35011 | securities, securities‑based derivatives
-- src:35012 | contracts or CIS units;
-- src:35014 | (iii) [Deleted by Act 4 of 2017]
-- src:35016 | (d) information relating to the financial performance of a
-- src:35017 | corporation or business trust, or otherwise;
-- src:35019 | (e) information that —
-- src:35021 | (i) a person proposes to enter into, or had
-- src:35022 | previously entered into, one or more
-- src:35023 | transactions or agreements in relation to any
-- src:35024 | securities, securities‑based derivatives contract
-- src:35025 | or CIS unit; or
-- src:35027 | (ii) a person has prepared or proposes to issue a
-- src:35028 | statement relating to any securities,
-- src:35029 | securities‑based derivatives contract or CIS
-- src:35030 | unit; and
-- src:35032 | (f) matters relating to the future;
@ref s 214(1) "information" (src:34993-35032)
GIVEN
    `the matter is a matter of supposition or another matter that is insufficiently definite to warrant being made known to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter a matter of supposition or another matter that is insufficiently definite to warrant being made known to the public?
    `the matter relates to the intentions, or the likely intentions, of a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter relate to the intentions, or the likely intentions, of a person?
    `the matter relates to negotiations or proposals with respect to commercial dealings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter relate to negotiations or proposals with respect to commercial dealings?
    `the matter relates to negotiations or proposals with respect to dealing in capital markets products that are securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter relate to negotiations or proposals with respect to dealing in capital markets products that are securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units?
    `the matter is information relating to the financial performance of a corporation or business trust, or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter information relating to the financial performance of a corporation or business trust, or otherwise?
    `the matter is information that a person proposes to enter into, or had previously entered into, transactions or agreements in relation to any securities, securities-based derivatives contract or CIS unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter information that a person proposes to enter into, or had previously entered into, one or more transactions or agreements in relation to any securities, securities-based derivatives contract or CIS unit?
    `the matter is information that a person has prepared or proposes to issue a statement relating to any securities, securities-based derivatives contract or CIS unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter information that a person has prepared or proposes to issue a statement relating to any securities, securities-based derivatives contract or CIS unit?
    `the matter relates to the future` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the matter relate to the future?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214(1) "information" the matter is information` MEANS
    IF `the matter is a matter of supposition or another matter that is insufficiently definite to warrant being made known to the public` OR `the matter relates to the intentions, or the likely intentions, of a person` OR `the matter relates to negotiations or proposals with respect to commercial dealings` OR `the matter relates to negotiations or proposals with respect to dealing in capital markets products that are securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units` OR `the matter is information relating to the financial performance of a corporation or business trust, or otherwise` OR `the matter is information that a person proposes to enter into, or had previously entered into, transactions or agreements in relation to any securities, securities-based derivatives contract or CIS unit` OR `the matter is information that a person has prepared or proposes to issue a statement relating to any securities, securities-based derivatives contract or CIS unit` OR `the matter relates to the future`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“information” includes"

-- src:35034 | “persons who commonly invest”, in relation to investment in
-- src:35035 | any kind of securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:35036 | or CIS units, means a section of the public that is accustomed,
-- src:35037 | or would be likely, to deal in securities, securities‑based
-- src:35038 | derivatives contracts or CIS units, or in a class of securities,
-- src:35039 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units, of that
-- src:35040 | kind;
@ref s 214(1) "persons who commonly invest" (src:35034-35040)
GIVEN
    `the persons are a section of the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the persons a section of the public?
    `the section of the public is accustomed to deal in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the section of the public accustomed to deal in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units, or in a class of them, of that kind?
    `the section of the public would be likely to deal in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the section of the public be likely to deal in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units, or in a class of them, of that kind?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214(1) "persons who commonly invest" the persons are persons who commonly invest` MEANS
    IF `the persons are a section of the public` AND (`the section of the public is accustomed to deal in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units of that kind` OR `the section of the public would be likely to deal in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units of that kind`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a section of the public that is accustomed, or would be likely, to deal in securities"

-- src:35042 | “purchase”, in relation to securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:35043 | or CIS units, includes a contract or arrangement under which
-- src:35044 | a party acquires an option or right from another party,
-- src:35045 | acquiring the option or right under the contract, or taking an
-- src:35046 | assignment of the option or right, whether or not on another’s
-- src:35047 | behalf;
@ref s 214(1) "purchase" (src:35042-35047)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a securities-based derivatives contract or a CIS unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a securities-based derivatives contract or a CIS unit?
    `the act is a contract or arrangement under which a party acquires an option or right from another party, acquiring the option or right under the contract, or taking an assignment of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act a contract or arrangement under which a party acquires an option or right from another party, acquiring the option or right under the contract, or taking an assignment of the option or right, whether or not on another's behalf?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214(1) "purchase" the act is a purchase of a securities-based derivatives contract or CIS unit` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a securities-based derivatives contract or a CIS unit` AND `the act is a contract or arrangement under which a party acquires an option or right from another party, acquiring the option or right under the contract, or taking an assignment of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“purchase”, in relation to securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units, includes"

-- FORK F-sell: the rendered text of "sell" reads "includes a contract or arrangement under which a party acquires an option or right from another party -- (a) grant or assign the option or right; or (b) take ... such action as releases the option or right".
-- The verb of the lead-in ("acquires") does not fit the limbs ("grant or assign", "take ... action"); it is encoded as the text reads (NOTES.md fork F-sell).
-- src:35049 | “sell”, in relation to securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS
-- src:35050 | units, includes a contract or arrangement under which a party
-- src:35051 | acquires an option or right from another party —
-- src:35056 | (a) grant or assign the option or right; or
-- src:35058 | (b) take, or cause to be taken, such action as releases the
-- src:35059 | option or right,
-- src:35061 | whether or not on another’s behalf;
@ref s 214(1) "sell" (src:35049-35061)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a securities-based derivatives contract or a CIS unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a securities-based derivatives contract or a CIS unit?
    `the act is a contract or arrangement under which a party acquires an option or right from another party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act a contract or arrangement under which a party acquires an option or right from another party?
    `the contract or arrangement is to grant or assign the option or right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement one to grant or assign the option or right?
    `the contract or arrangement is to take, or cause to be taken, such action as releases the option or right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract or arrangement one to take, or cause to be taken, such action as releases the option or right?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 214(1) "sell" the act is a sale of a securities-based derivatives contract or CIS unit` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a securities-based derivatives contract or a CIS unit` AND `the act is a contract or arrangement under which a party acquires an option or right from another party` AND (`the contract or arrangement is to grant or assign the option or right` OR `the contract or arrangement is to take, or cause to be taken, such action as releases the option or right`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“sell”, in relation to securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units, includes"

