§ `s 215: information generally available`

-- src:35086 | 215. For the purposes of this Division, information is generally
-- src:35087 | available if —
-- src:35089 | (a) it consists of readily observable matter;
-- src:35091 | (b) without limiting paragraph (a) —
-- src:35093 | (i) it has been made known in a manner that would, or
-- src:35094 | would be likely to, bring it to the attention of any of
-- src:35095 | the following classes of persons:
-- src:35097 | (A) persons who commonly invest in securities of a
-- src:35098 | kind of which the price or value might be
-- src:35099 | affected by the information;
-- src:35101 | (B) persons who commonly invest in
-- src:35102 | securities‑based derivatives contracts of a
-- src:35107 | kind of which the price or value might be
-- src:35108 | affected by the information;
-- src:35110 | (C) persons who commonly invest in CIS units of a
-- src:35111 | kind of which the price or value might be
-- src:35112 | affected by the information; and
-- src:35114 | (ii) since it was so made known, a reasonable period for
-- src:35115 | it to be disseminated among such persons has
-- src:35116 | elapsed; or
-- src:35118 | (c) it consists of deductions, conclusions or inferences made or
-- src:35119 | drawn from either or both of the following:
-- src:35121 | (i) information referred to in paragraph (a);
-- src:35123 | (ii) information made known as referred to in
-- src:35124 | paragraph (b)(i).
@ref s 215 (src:35086-35124)
GIVEN
    `the information consists of readily observable matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information consist of readily observable matter?
    `the information has been made known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly invest in securities of a kind affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the information been made known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly invest in securities of a kind of which the price or value might be affected by the information?
    `the information has been made known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly invest in securities-based derivatives contracts of a kind affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the information been made known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly invest in securities-based derivatives contracts of a kind of which the price or value might be affected by the information?
    `the information has been made known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly invest in CIS units of a kind affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the information been made known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly invest in CIS units of a kind of which the price or value might be affected by the information?
    `since it was so made known, a reasonable period for it to be disseminated among such persons has elapsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since it was so made known, has a reasonable period for it to be disseminated among such persons elapsed?
    `the information consists of deductions, conclusions or inferences made or drawn from readily observable matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information consist of deductions, conclusions or inferences made or drawn from information consisting of readily observable matter?
    `the information consists of deductions, conclusions or inferences made or drawn from information made known as referred to in paragraph (b)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information consist of deductions, conclusions or inferences made or drawn from information made known as referred to in paragraph (b)(i)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215 the information is generally available` MEANS
    IF `the information consists of readily observable matter` OR ((`the information has been made known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly invest in securities of a kind affected` OR `the information has been made known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly invest in securities-based derivatives contracts of a kind affected` OR `the information has been made known in a manner that would, or would be likely to, bring it to the attention of persons who commonly invest in CIS units of a kind affected`) AND `since it was so made known, a reasonable period for it to be disseminated among such persons has elapsed`) OR `the information consists of deductions, conclusions or inferences made or drawn from readily observable matter` OR `the information consists of deductions, conclusions or inferences made or drawn from information made known as referred to in paragraph (b)(i)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "information is generally available if" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

§ `s 216: material effect on price or value of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units`

-- src:35131 | 216. For the purposes of this Division, a reasonable person would
-- src:35132 | be taken to expect information to have a material effect on the price or
-- src:35133 | value of securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS
-- src:35134 | units, if the information would, or would be likely to, influence any of
-- src:35135 | the following persons in deciding whether or not to subscribe for, buy
-- src:35136 | or sell those securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS
-- src:35137 | units:
-- src:35139 | (a) the persons who commonly invest in the securities,
-- src:35140 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units;
-- src:35142 | (b) any one or more classes of persons who constitute the
-- src:35143 | persons mentioned in paragraph (a).
@ref s 216 (src:35131-35143)
GIVEN
    `the information would, or would be likely to, influence the persons who commonly invest in deciding whether or not to subscribe for, buy or sell the securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the information, or would it be likely to, influence the persons who commonly invest in the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units in deciding whether or not to subscribe for, buy or sell them?
    `the information would, or would be likely to, influence one or more classes of the persons who commonly invest in deciding whether or not to subscribe for, buy or sell the securities, contracts or units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the information, or would it be likely to, influence any one or more classes of persons who constitute the persons who commonly invest in deciding whether or not to subscribe for, buy or sell the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216 a reasonable person would be taken to expect the information to have a material effect on the price or value` MEANS
    IF `the information would, or would be likely to, influence the persons who commonly invest in deciding whether or not to subscribe for, buy or sell the securities, contracts or units` OR `the information would, or would be likely to, influence one or more classes of the persons who commonly invest in deciding whether or not to subscribe for, buy or sell the securities, contracts or units`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "would be taken to expect information to have a material effect on the price or value of securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units, if the information would, or would be likely to, influence" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

§ `s 217: trading and procuring trading`

-- src:35150 | 217.—(1) For the purposes of this Division, trading in any
-- src:35151 | securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units, that
-- src:35152 | is ordinarily permitted on an organised market is taken to be
-- src:35157 | permitted on that organised market even though trading in such
-- src:35158 | securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units (as the
-- src:35159 | case may be) on that organised market is suspended.
@ref s 217(1) (src:35150-35159)
GIVEN
    `trading in the securities, contracts or units is ordinarily permitted on an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is trading in the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or CIS units ordinarily permitted on an organised market?
    `trading in them on that organised market is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is trading in them on that organised market suspended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 217(1) trading is taken to be permitted on the organised market` MEANS
    IF `trading in the securities, contracts or units is ordinarily permitted on an organised market`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- "even though trading ... is suspended": the suspension does not change the answer (the input about suspension is read and ignored here on purpose)
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "trading in any securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts or CIS units, that is ordinarily permitted on an organised market is taken to be permitted"

-- src:35163 | (2) For the purposes of this Division but without limiting the
-- src:35164 | meaning that the expression “procure” has apart from this section, if a
-- src:35165 | person incites, induces, or encourages an act or omission by another
-- src:35166 | person, the firstmentioned person is taken to procure the act or
-- src:35167 | omission by the other person.
@ref s 217(2) (src:35163-35167)
GIVEN
    `the person incites an act or omission by another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person incite an act or omission by another person?
    `the person induces an act or omission by another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person induce an act or omission by another person?
    `the person encourages an act or omission by another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person encourage an act or omission by another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 217(2) the person is taken to procure the act or omission by the other person` MEANS
    IF `the person incites an act or omission by another person` OR `the person induces an act or omission by another person` OR `the person encourages an act or omission by another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "without limiting the meaning that the expression “procure” has apart from this section"
